.TH zcfan 1

.SH NAME
zcfan - zero-configuration fan control daemon for ThinkPads

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zcfan
is a minimal, zero-configuration fan control daemon for ThinkPads. It uses
an arithmetic average of available temperature readings for fan control. When
CPU-core readings can be identified, only those are averaged; otherwise CPU
readings are preferred, with a fallback to all readable temperature inputs.
The fan-control temperature is the maximum of the core average and the ACPI/EC
sensor reading, the same reading the platform's critical-shutdown trip reacts
to. Die/package readings are deliberately excluded: they spike hotter and
faster than the trip sensor. Unavailable and non-positive readings are
ignored. The set of readable, non-ignored temperature inputs is re-checked
roughly once per second, so hwmon drivers that register after
.B zcfan
has started (for example, coretemp being autoloaded by udev during boot) are
picked up automatically.

.SH OPTIONS
.B zcfan
does not take any options. If any are provided, a help message will be printed
and
.B zcfan
will exit.

.SH CONFIGURATION

.SS USAGE

.B zcfan
has the following default fan states:

.RS
.TS
tab(;);
l l l l.
Config name;thinkpad_acpi fan level;Default trip temperature (C);Default debounce (s)
_
max_temp;full-speed;90;10
med_temp;4;80;30
low_temp;1;70;60
.TE
.RE

You can optionally override this configuration at
.I /etc/zcfan.conf
with your desired threshold values in the following format:

.RS
.EX
max_temp 85
med_temp 70
low_temp 55
.EE
.RE

If no trip temperature is reached, the fan will be turned off.

The number of consecutive seconds the average temperature must stay above a
level's trip temperature before that level is engaged can be set per level with
the
.I max_debounce_secs
,
.I med_debounce_secs
, and
.I low_debounce_secs
parameters. A value of 0 or 1 engages the level immediately. For example:

.RS
.EX
max_debounce_secs 1
med_debounce_secs 3
low_debounce_secs 5
.EE
.RE

.SS HYSTERESIS

We will only reduce the fan level again once:
.IP "1." 3
The average temperature is now at least
.I temp_hysteresis
Celsius below the trip point (default 20C), and
.IP "2." 3
At least 3 seconds have elapsed since the initial trip.
.PP

This avoids unnecessary fluctuations in fan speed.

.SS DEBOUNCE

Conversely, before we engage a higher fan level, the average temperature must
remain above that level's trip point for a number of consecutive seconds set by
.I low_debounce_secs
,
.I med_debounce_secs
, and
.I max_debounce_secs
(defaults 60, 30, and 10). This prevents brief temperature spikes from needlessly
spinning the fans up. A value of 0 or 1 engages the level immediately.

The debounce is bypassed at 95C and above: the maximum fan level is engaged
immediately, to stay clear of the firmware's critical shutdown temperature.

.SS WATCHDOG

The kernel watchdog is reset every 120 seconds by default, but a
smaller value can be selected in the
.I /etc/zcfan.conf
config file with the syntax

.RS
.EX
watchdog_secs 10
.EE
.RE

Along with each watchdog reset, zcfan verifies that the EC has not reverted
to its own automatic fan control, and re-asserts the held level if it has.

.SH DEPENDENCIES
.B thinkpad-acpi
must be loaded with
.IR fan_control=1.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR thinkfan (1)

